%I A399174 #17 Oct 21 2026 20:07:18
%S A399174 5,7,11,13,17,8741,8747,8753,8779,9461,9463,9467,9473,9533,9539,9697,
%T A399174 9721,9733,92861,92863,92867,92893,93077,93083,93089,93139,93151,
%U A399174 93187,93199,93229,93241,93251,93253,93257,94397,94399,94439,94463,94477,94513,94529,94541
%N A399174 Primes p for which pi_{24;19,23}(p) - pi_{24;1,5}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A399174 Let H be a proper subgroup of (Z/NZ)* containing all the squares, and S != H be a coset of H. Assuming the generalized Riemann hypothesis (GRH) and the Grand Simplicity Hypothesis (GSH; called LI in page 29 of Greg Martin's 2010 link), then pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x) occurs more often than not: the set {pi_{N;S}(x) > pi_{N;H}(x)} has logarithmic density greater than 1/2. This phenomenon is called "Chebyshev's bias".
%C A399174 Here we have N = 24, H = {1,5} and S = {19,23}. There are 153852 known terms, among which a(153094..153852) = 1018491958181-1023709414961 are from a single sign-changing zone. No furthur terms up to p = 1029527569223, for which pi_{24;19,23}(p) - pi_{24;1,5}(p) = 8660.
%H A399174 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399174/b399174.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..76356</a> (all terms up to 10^11)
%H A399174 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A399174 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A399174 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A399174 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399174/a399174.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..153852</a>.
%H A399174 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A399174 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==5, k--); if(p%24==19||p%24==23, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A399174 Races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*:
%Y A399174 H = {1,5}: A398377 (S = {7,11}), A399143 (S = {13,17}), this sequence (S = {19,23});
%Y A399174 H = {1,13}: A297355 (S = {5,17}), A297357 (S = {7,19});
%Y A399174 H = {1,17}: A297448 (S = {5,13}), A295354 (S = {7,23});
%Y A399174 H = {1,19}: A398234 (S = {5,23}), A398235 (S = {7,13}), A398236 (S = {11,17});
%Y A399174 H = {1,23}: A401243 (S = {5,19}), A401244 (S = {7,17}), A401245 (S = {11,13}).
